Changes: condensed and rewritten into three self-contained, read-only skills;
removed Claude-specific tools, agents, workflows, model selection, mandatory
report writes and cross-plugin dependencies. Added local-only execution rules,
explicit authorization boundaries, snapshot/line evidence, refutation and
confidence requirements, and bounded negative conclusions. Rewrote examples to
require actual security impact rather than classify CORS wildcards, debug schema
visibility, pre-umask modes or algorithm names by themselves as vulnerabilities.
Added a Wevir manifest, localized listing, README and original icon.

